# Notes

See [custom applications](/docs/applications/custom/).

A small custom app: authored `main.roc` owns HTTP, Rocci templates render the
page, and SQLite stores notes. Use this when you want Roc-centered development
with `.rocci` views, before the Datastar gallery or Snake.

This app is **docs-only** on rocci.dev.

See the [source tree](/examples/notes/source/).

## Run locally

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/custom/notes
```

Pass `--no-window` to serve on [http://127.0.0.1:8000](http://127.0.0.1:8000).
SQLite state is `examples/rocci/custom/notes/notes.db` unless `DB_PATH` is set.

## Smoke

```sh
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/ | grep -E 'id="notes"|Add a note'
```
